filex-office-editor (scripts/x2t), BRF Tech, 2026-11-08: <cfloat> in the
spreadsheet reader's SheetData.cpp.

OOXML/XlsxFormat/Worksheets/SheetData.cpp compares a cell's value with
DBL_MAX and does not include <cfloat>. With glibc's and libstdc++'s headers
another header brings it in; at v10.0.0.169, with emscripten's libc++, none
does, and DocxFormatLib stops: "use of undeclared identifier 'DBL_MAX'"
(measured). The include is added; nothing else changes. (Not in
OOXML/XlsxFormat/Common.cpp, which defines a DBL_MAX of its own, a number of
digits.)

git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line on.

diff --git a/OOXML/XlsxFormat/Worksheets/SheetData.cpp b/OOXML/XlsxFormat/Worksheets/SheetData.cpp
index 9a8142ad..5f80e4b6 100644
--- a/OOXML/XlsxFormat/Worksheets/SheetData.cpp
+++ b/OOXML/XlsxFormat/Worksheets/SheetData.cpp
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
  * SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
  */
 
+#include <cfloat>
 #include "../Workbook/Workbook.h"
 
 #include "../Common.h"
